outputs.L2:
A memory apparatus comprises:

- multiple bank groups, each containing at least one bank;
- first and second buses, both connected to the bank groups;
- a toggle-signal generator configured to produce a first signal that changes state in response to a column-command signal and a second signal whose logic state is complementary to that of the first signal;
- a column-command transmitter configured to route a read-command signal or a write-command signal through the first bus when the first signal is active and through the second bus when the second signal is active; and
- a column-address transmitter configured to send one or more column-address signals associated with the read-command signal or write-command signal over whichever of the first and second buses carries that command signal.

counterfactuals.output:
1. **A memory device comprising:**

a memory cell array including a plurality of memory banks partitioned into a first bank group and a second bank group;

a first command/address bus associated with the first bank group;

a second command/address bus associated with the second bank group;

a toggle-signal generation circuit configured to generate a toggle signal that alternates between a first state and a second state in response to receipt of successive column commands;

a column-command routing circuit configured to route a received column command to one of the first command/address bus or the second command/address bus based at least in part on the toggle signal; and

a column-address transmission circuit configured to transmit a column address corresponding to the received column command over the same one of the first command/address bus or the second command/address bus to which the received column command is routed,

wherein the column-command routing circuit and the column-address transmission circuit are configured to cause successive column commands, together with their corresponding column addresses, to be conveyed alternately via the first command/address bus and the second command/address bus for execution by a selected memory bank of the first bank group or the second bank group.
